#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "Boiled fiddleheads.  Not bad, but would be better sauteed in butter."
msgstr "삶은 고비입니다. 나쁘지는 않지만, 버터에 재빨리 볶았다면 더 좋았을텐데요."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "sauteed fiddleheads"
msgid_plural "sauteed fiddleheads"
msgstr[0] "고비 볶음"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'sauteed fiddleheads'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "Fiddleheads sauteed in fat.  Tender and delicious."
msgstr "지방에 볶은 고비. 부드럽고 맛있습니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "wheat cereal"
msgid_plural "wheat cereals"
msgstr[0] "통밀 시리얼"

#. ~ Description for wheat cereal
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Whole-grain wheat cereal.  It's surprisingly good, and allegedly good for "
"your heart."
msgstr "통밀 시리얼. 놀라울 정도로 맛있고, 심장에도 좋습니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'wheat'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Raw wheat, not very tasty."
msgstr "생 밀알. 별로 먹을만한게 못됩니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "raw spaghetti pasta"
msgid_plural "raw spaghetti pasta"
msgstr[0] "생 스파게티 파스타"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'raw spaghetti pasta'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"A type of pasta usually used when preparing spaghetti.  It could be eaten "
"raw if you're desperate, but is much better cooked."
msgstr "주로 스파게티를 만들 때 쓰는 파스타입니다. 정말 급하다면 이대로 먹을 수도 있지만, 요리해서 먹는게 더 나을겁니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "raw lasagne pasta"
msgid_plural "raw lasagne pasta"
msgstr[0] "생 라자냐"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'raw lasagne pasta'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"A pasta sheet used in making lasagne.  It could be eaten raw if you're "
"desperate, but is much better cooked."
msgstr "라자냐를 만들 때 쓰는 파스타입니다. 정말 급하다면 이대로 먹을 수도 있지만, 요리해서 먹는게 더 나을겁니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "boiled noodles"
msgid_plural "boiled noodles"
msgstr[0] "끓인 국수"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'boiled noodles'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Fresh wet noodles.  Fairly bland, but fills you up."
msgstr "신선하고 촉촉한 면발입니다. 단조로운 메뉴지만, 배불리 먹을 수 있습니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "raw macaroni"
msgid_plural "raw macaroni"
msgstr[0] "생 마카로니"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'raw macaroni'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "It could be eaten raw if you're desperate, but is much better cooked."
msgstr "절망적인 상황이라면 생으로 먹을 수 있습니다만, 요리해서 먹는게 훨씬 좋습니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "mac & cheese"
msgid_plural "mac & cheese"
msgstr[0] "치즈 마카로니"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'mac & cheese'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "When the cheese starts flowing, Kraft gets your noodle going."
msgstr "치즈가 흐르기 시작할 때, 크래프트의 면발 맛도 같이 흐릅니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "flour"
msgid_plural "flour"
msgstr[0] "밀가루"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'flour'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "This enriched white flour is useful for baking."
msgstr "제빵에 쓰이는 하얀 밀가루."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "oatmeal"
msgid_plural "oatmeal"
msgstr[0] "오트밀"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'oatmeal'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Dry flakes of flattened grain.  Tasty and nutritious when cooked, it also "
"doubles as food for horses while dry."
msgstr "귀리를 갈아 만든 건조한 가루. 조리하면 배부르고 맛있게 먹을 수 있고, 건조된 상태에선 말 먹이로도 쓰인다."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'oats'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Raw oats."
msgstr "생 귀리."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "cooked oatmeal"
msgid_plural "cooked oatmeal"
msgstr[0] "오트밀 (요리됨)"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'cooked oatmeal'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"A filling and nutritious New England classic that has sustained pioneers and"
" captains of industry alike."
msgstr "개척민과 산업역군을 지탱해주던 전통 뉴잉글랜드 요리. 배 채우기엔 딱 좋다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "deluxe cooked oatmeal"
msgid_plural "deluxe cooked oatmeal"
msgstr[0] "특제 오트밀 요리"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'deluxe cooked oatmeal'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"A filling and nutritious New England classic that has been improved with the"
" addition of extra wholesome ingredients."
msgstr "건강에 좋은 재료를 넣어서 만든 전통 뉴잉글랜드 요리. 배 채우기엔 딱 좋다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "pancake"
msgid_plural "pancakes"
msgstr[0] "팬케이크"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pancake'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Fluffy and delicious pancakes with real maple syrup."
msgstr "보들거리고 맛있는 팬케이크. 진짜 메이플 시럽이 뿌려져 있습니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "fruit pancake"
msgid_plural "fruit pancakes"
msgstr[0] "과일 팬케이크"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'fruit pancake'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Fluffy and delicious pancakes with real maple syrup, made sweeter and "
"healthier with the addition of wholesome fruit."
msgstr "보들거리고 맛있는 팬케이크에 엄선된 과일을 넣어 영양과 맛을 강화시켰습니다. 진짜 메이플 시럽이 뿌려져 있습니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "French toast"
msgid_plural "French toasts"
msgstr[0] "프렌치 토스트"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'French toast'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Slices of bread dipped in a milk and egg mixture then fried."
msgstr "빵을 얇게 썰어서 우유와 달걀을 섞은 물에 담근 뒤 구운 음식."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "waffle"
msgid_plural "waffles"
msgstr[0] "와플"

#. ~ Description for waffle
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Hey it's waffle time, it's waffle time.  Won't you have some waffles of "
"mine?"
msgstr ""
"이봐 지금 와플 시간이야, 와플 시간이라고. 내 와플 좀 들겠나?\n"
"(역주: 미국 드라마 스크럽스(Scrubs)의 패러디.)"

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "fruit waffle"
msgid_plural "fruit waffles"
msgstr[0] "과일 와플"

#. ~ Description for fruit waffle
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Crunchy and delicious waffles with real maple syrup, made sweeter and "
"healthier with the addition of wholesome fruit."
msgstr "진짜 메이플 시럽을 곁들인 바삭바삭하고 맛있는 와플로, 건강에 좋은 과일을 더해서 달면서도 건강에 좋은 음식이 되었습니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
#: data/mods/My_Sweet_Cataclysm/sweet_monsters.json
msgid "cracker"
msgid_plural "crackers"
msgstr[0] "크래커"

#. ~ Description for cracker
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Dry and salty, these crackers will leave you quite thirsty."
msgstr "건조하고 짭짤한 크래커 과자입니다. 먹으면 금세 목이 마르게 됩니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "fruit pie"
msgid_plural "fruit pies"
msgstr[0] "과일 파이"

#. ~ Description for fruit pie
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "A delicious baked pie with a sweet fruit filling."
msgstr "과일로 채워져 맛있게 구워진 파이입니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "cheese pizza"
msgid_plural "cheese pizzas"
msgstr[0] "치즈 피자"

#. ~ Description for cheese pizza
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "A delicious pizza with molten cheese on top."
msgstr "녹은 치즈를 위에 올린 맛있는 피자."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "granola"
msgid_plural "granola"
msgstr[0] "그래놀라"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'granola'}
#. ~ Description for gluten free granola
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
#: data/mods/Tolerate_This/comestibles.json
msgid ""
"A tasty and nutritious mixture of oats, honey, and other ingredients that "
"has been baked until crisp."
msgstr "귀리, 꿀, 그리고 여러가지 다른 재료들의 혼합물을 바삭해질 때까지 구운 과자. 맛있고 영양가가 높다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "maple pie"
msgid_plural "maple pies"
msgstr[0] "메이플 파이"

#. ~ Description for maple pie
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "A sweet and delicious baked pie with pure maple syrup."
msgstr "100% 메이플 시럽을 넣어 구운 달고 맛있는 파이입니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "fast noodles"
msgid_plural "fast noodles"
msgstr[0] "라면"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'fast noodles'}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "So-called ramen noodles.  Can be eaten raw."
msgstr "'라면'이라고 부르는 국수입니다. 날로 먹을 수도 있습니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "cloutie dumpling"
msgid_plural "cloutie dumplings"
msgstr[0] "클로티 덤플링"

#. ~ Description for cloutie dumpling
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"This traditional Scottish treat is a sweet and filling little boiled cake "
"studded with dried fruit."
msgstr "말린 과일을 잔뜩 넣고 삶아서 만든 스코틀랜드 전통 빵. 달콤하고 허기를 채워준다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "brioche"
msgid_plural "brioches"
msgstr[0] "브리오슈"

#. ~ Description for brioche
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Filling bread buns, taste good with tea on a Sunday morning breakfast."
msgstr "배를 채워주는 빵으로, 일요일 아침식사로 차와 함께 먹으면 맛있습니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "sponge cake"
msgid_plural "sponge cakes"
msgstr[0] "푹신 케이크"

#. ~ Description for sponge cake
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Plain, fluffy cake for the proletariat."
msgstr "프롤레타리아를 위한 장식없고 푹신한 케이크."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "space cake"
msgid_plural "space cakes"
msgstr[0] "우주 케이크"

#. ~ Description for space cake
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "This cake's destiny is to take you on a gnarly trip."
msgstr "이 케이크는 당신을 끝내주는 여행에 인도할겁니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "brownie"
msgid_plural "brownies"
msgstr[0] "브라우니"

#. ~ Description for brownie
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "A rich chocolate brownie, just like how grandma used to bake them."
msgstr "초콜릿이 풍부한 브라우니. 할머니가 구워주시던 바로 그 맛입니다."

#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "'special' brownie"
msgid_plural "'special' brownies"
msgstr[0] "\"특제\" 브라우니"

#. ~ Description for {'str': "'special' brownie"}
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "This is definitely not how grandma used to bake them."
msgstr "이것은 할머니가 구워주시던 브라우니와는 전혀 다릅니다."

#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "corpse"
msgid_plural "corpses"
msgstr[0] "시체"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'corpse'} when FLAG matches FIELD_DRESS
#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'corpse'} when FLAG matches
#. FIELD_DRESS_FAILED
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "carcass"
msgid_plural "carcasses"
msgstr[0] "시체"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'corpse'} when FLAG matches SKINNED
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
#, c-format
msgid "skinned %s"
msgid_plural "skinned %s"
msgstr[0] "껍질벗긴 %s"

#. ~ Conditional name for {'str': 'corpse'} when FLAG matches QUARTERED
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "carcass quarter"
msgid_plural "carcass quarters"
msgstr[0] "4분한 시체"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "A dead body."
msgstr "시체."

#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "desiccated corpse"
msgid_plural "desiccated corpses"
msgstr[0] "건조 시체"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'desiccated corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid ""
"A dead body, badly mangled and desiccated.  It seems whatever killed him did"
" so with a gigantic claw."
msgstr "엉망으로 찢겨지고 박살난 시체입니다. 이걸 죽인 자는 거대한 발톱을 가진 것 같습니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "A dead human body."
msgstr "인간 시체."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "A dead body of a middle-aged man."
msgstr "중년 남자의 시체."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "A dead body of a young woman."
msgstr "어린 여자의 시체."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "A dead body of a little boy."
msgstr "작은 소년의 시체."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "A dead body of a little girl."
msgstr "작은 소녀의 시체."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid ""
"The dead body of a small child.  Their corpse bears a calm facial "
"expression, as if they died instantly."
msgstr "어린아이의 시체. 얼굴 표정이 평안한 것이, 고통을 느낄 새도 없이 사망한 것 같습니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid ""
"The dead body of a child, riddled by bullets to the extent that you can no "
"longer tell their gender."
msgstr "성별을 알아보기 힘들만큼 총탄을 맞은 아이의 시체."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid ""
"A dead body of an old woman.  Both of her earlobes are torn, several fingers"
" on her hands have been chopped off, and several teeth have been knocked "
"out."
msgstr "나이든 여자의 시체. 양 귓불이 찢겨지고, 손가락 몇개가 잘려나갔으며, 이빨도 몇 개 뽑혔습니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "A dead body, coated in congealed blood."
msgstr "피가 엉겨붙은 시체."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid ""
"A dead body with a frightful grimace.  He appears to have been horribly "
"mangled prior to his death."
msgstr "끔찍한 고통이 드러난 시체. 죽기 전에 잔혹하게 저며진 것 같습니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "An awful, almost unidentifiable mass of charred flesh."
msgstr "지독하게, 거의 알아볼 수 없을 정도로 불태워진 살덩이."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid "A dead body with a gaping stab wound in its back."
msgstr "등 뒤에서 찔린 상처가 남아있는 시체."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid ""
"The dead body of a person.  Their forehead bears a large bullet entrance "
"wound.  An even larger exit wound is present on the back of their head."
msgstr "누군가의 시체. 머리 앞쪽에 커다란 총상이 있습니다. 머리 뒤쪽의 총상은 더 큽니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid ""
"The upper half of a dead body, as if torn apart with enormous force.  Some "
"organs are hanging out."
msgstr "시체의 상반신 부분으로, 무지막지한 힘으로 찢겨져나갔습니다. 몇몇 장기가 매달려있습니다."

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'corpse'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/corpses.json
msgid ""
"A half-decapitated dead body.  It is unclear what could have caused such a "
"wound."
msgstr "반쯤 참수된 시체. 무엇이 이런 상처를 만들었는지는 확실치 않습니다."

#: data/json/items/corpses/inactive_bots.json
msgid "inactive EMP hack"
msgid_plural "inactive EMP hacks"
msgstr[0] "EMP 맨핵 (꺼짐)"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for {'str': 'inactive EMP hack'}.
#: data/json/items/corpses/inactive_bots.json
msgid "The EMP hack flies from your hand and surveys the area!"
msgstr "EMP 맨핵이 손에서 날아올라 주변을 관찰한다!"

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for {'str': 'inactive EMP hack'}.
#: data/json/items/corpses/inactive_bots.json
msgid "You misprogram the EMP hack; take cover!"
msgstr "EMP 맨핵을 잘못 프로그래밍했다. 모두 다 엎드려!"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'inactive EMP hack'}
#: data/json/items/corpses/inactive_bots.json
msgid ""
"This is an inactive EMP hack.  EMP hacks are fist-sized robots that fly "
"through the air.  This one contains an EMP grenade and attacks by flying at "
"its target and detonating.  Use this item to reprogram and release the EMP "
"hack.  Electronics and computer skill determines if the targeting matrix is "
"reprogrammed successfully."
msgstr ""
"비활성화된 EMP 맨핵입니다. EMP 맨핵은 하늘을 날아다니는 주먹만한 크기의 로봇으로, EMP 수류탄이 담겨있어 목표를 추적해 "
"폭발합니다. 사용하면 EMP 맨핵을 재프로그래밍한 후 날려보냅니다. 전자공학 및 컴퓨터 기술이 목표 조준 시스템이 제대로 "
"재프로그래밍되었는지를 결정합니다."

#: data/json/items/corpses/inactive_bots.json
msgid "inactive C-4 hack"
msgid_plural "inactive C-4 hacks"
msgstr[0] "C-4 맨핵 (꺼짐)"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for {'str': 'inactive C-4 hack'}.
#: data/json/items/corpses/inactive_bots.json
msgid "The C-4 hack flies from your hand and surveys the area!"
msgstr "C-4 맨핵이 손에서 날아올라 주변을 관찰한다!"

